        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "Direct-to-origin bypass of CloudFront security controls may occur when an attacker discovers the API Gateway endpoint URL and sends requests directly, bypassing WAFv2, HSTS, CSP, and CDN-layer rate limiting.",
            "markdown": "Implement API Gateway resource policy restricting invocations to CloudFront IP ranges or require a secret header set by CloudFront that Lambda validates; alternatively enforce mutual TLS between CloudFront and API Gateway."
